 "asked_at": "2026-10-18T00:45+08:00",
 "answer": "**Bring a well-fitting N95, KN95, KF94 or FFP2 mask, but you probably don’t need to wear it for a brief walk outside if you’re otherwise healthy.** Singapore’s forecast for **Sunday, October 18** is *unhealthy to very unhealthy* air quality, so avoid a long or strenuous outdoor outing. Conditions can change by the hour. ([weather.gov.sg](https://www.weather.gov.sg/haze-situation-update-17-october-2026/))\n\nBefore you go out, check your area’s **latest 1-hour PM2.5 reading** on Singapore’s haze site or myENV app. If it’s **High**, people who are elderly, pregnant, or have heart or lung conditions should avoid going out; if going out is necessary, a well-fitting N95 or equivalent can reduce exposure. If it’s **Very High**, everyone should minimise time outdoors, and a mask can help when going out is unavoidable. A surgical mask is not effective at filtering fine haze particles. ([moh.gov.sg](https://www.moh.gov.sg/others/haze/))",
